cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this course material, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "Blockrophage: Macrophage Biology in vitro, in vivo, in silico. An open block course"
abstract: >-
  Open course material for a four-week block course on macrophage biology at
  D-BIOL, ETH Zürich: course script, schedule, lab protocols, background reading,
  analysis code and a single-file AI companion. Students polarize RAW 264.7
  macrophages, challenge them with danger signals and compare the in vitro states
  with tissue macrophages in a published single-cell dataset.
authors:
  - family-names: Zindel
    given-names: Joel
    affiliation: "ETH Zürich"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/TizzuLab/Blockrophage"
url: "https://zindellab.ch/blockcourse.html"
keywords:
  - macrophages
  - immunology
  - teaching
  - open educational resources
  - RAW 264.7
  - single-cell RNA sequencing
